# Cache policy for everything Cloudflare serves out of dist/.
#
# Workers Static Assets answers with `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` unless
# told otherwise, and that default is why this site has never needed a purge step
# on release: the ETag is a hash of the file, a deploy changes it, and the next
# request revalidates straight into the new bytes. The default is the right
# answer for anything whose URL outlives its contents, which is why exactly one
# path below overrides it.
#
# This file is configuration rather than content. Cloudflare reads it out of the
# assets directory and does not serve it (/_headers is a 404), and Astro copies
# public/ verbatim, so it needs no build step. Verified to apply through
# `env.ASSETS.fetch()` despite `run_worker_first: true` in wrangler.jsonc, which
# puts worker.js in front of every request including these.

# Astro content-hashes everything it emits here, so the URL changes whenever the
# bytes do: a release does not invalidate the old URL, it stops referencing it.
# That is what makes a year safe, and tests/cache-headers.test.mjs checks the
# hashing rather than trusting it, because an unhashed file under this path would
# be a stale copy nobody can reach into a browser and remove.
#
# `immutable` is the half that earns its keep. Without it the browser still
# revalidates on reload, and a conditional request that can only ever answer 304
# is the one round trip the rest of this policy cannot avoid. Nearly every byte
# the site loads is under here: the CSS bundle, ten woff2 faces, every processed
# image.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Everything else is left on the default deliberately, and the test pins that
# too, so this stays a decision rather than an omission somebody tidies up:
#
#   /images/*, /documents/*  Decap's media folders. Editors upload under their
#                            own filenames and can replace a file under the same
#                            name, so a cached copy goes stale with no URL change
#                            to shake it loose. Four files today, against a
#                            wrong logo nobody can purge.
#   *.html                   The pointer to the hashed assets above. Stale here
#                            means stale everywhere.
#   /meetings.ics            The daily rebuild is the entire freshness mechanism
#                            for a cancelled meeting, and calendar subscribers
#                            sit downstream of it.
#   /admin/*                 Decap ships numbered chunks (4025.decap-cms.js),
#                            not content-hashed ones.
